## Model card
- **Name:** Big Pickle (limited-time Free on OpenCode Zen; no separate Free-suffixed ID)
- **Short description:** A closed, undisclosed stealth reasoning-model alias served by OpenCode Zen for coding-agent, multi-step problem-solving, and tool-use workloads. The underlying developer and model are not publicly identified. 
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen `opencode/big-pickle` through `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/chat/completions`; OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions API. 
- **Release / knowledge:** 2025-10-17 release metadata; models.dev lists knowledge as 2025-01, but no vendor-authored cutoff was found. 
- **IDs:** `opencode/big-pickle`; no separate `opencode/big-pickle-free` ID exists in the published Zen model table—the unsuffixed ID is the limited-time Free offering. 
- **Context window:** 200,000 tokens total; 160,000 maximum input and 32,000 maximum output, verified from models.dev catalog metadata rather than a retrieval benchmark. 
- **Modalities:** Text input and text output; no image, audio, video, or PDF input; reasoning yes; tool calls yes; structured output yes; JSON mode not separately documented. 
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-05):** US$0 input, US$0 output, and US$0 cached read per 1M tokens; cached write is not listed. Free for a limited time; collected data may be used to improve the model during the free period. 
- **Architecture:** Undisclosed closed-weight architecture; models.dev marks `open_weights = false`. Parameter count, active parameters, MoE design, underlying model identity, and license are not publicly disclosed. 
